you come and build
container-- no,

00:24:30.936 --> 00:24:32.500
you should think like kernel--

00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:35.600
there's an enterprise who comes
with a pure [? private ?] cloud

00:24:35.600 --> 00:24:38.030
experience, redesigned
the platform

00:24:38.030 --> 00:24:40.280
with the next generation
offering as a greenfield,

00:24:40.280 --> 00:24:43.280
built GCP and the native
services from infrastructure,

00:24:43.280 --> 00:24:46.460
and wrote our own
architecture by leveraging

00:24:46.460 --> 00:24:48.440
the entire cloud-nativeness.

00:24:48.440 --> 00:24:51.492
And I think that is where,
as an example-- and I believe

00:24:51.492 --> 00:24:52.200
we learned a lot.

00:24:52.200 --> 00:24:53.540
Google learned a
lot, and we were

00:24:53.540 --> 00:24:55.248
in this journey from
the last three years

00:24:55.248 --> 00:24:57.260
where I think we have
complemented each other.

00:24:57.260 --> 00:25:00.830
And today we stand
where, I'll tell you--

00:25:00.830 --> 00:25:03.344
I could say that we are
live, it's been one year.

00:25:03.344 --> 00:25:04.760
But we have been
live three years.

00:25:04.760 --> 00:25:08.390
I have 6,000 people
using Google in Kronos.

00:25:08.390 --> 00:25:11.240
We have literally, if
I count internally,

00:25:11.240 --> 00:25:15.500
close to more than a million
employees in the system.

00:25:15.500 --> 00:25:17.360
We have close to
4,000, 5,000 tenants

00:25:17.360 --> 00:25:19.700
internally being
leveraged by engining

00:25:19.700 --> 00:25:21.830
and our internal organizations.

00:25:21.830 --> 00:25:24.074
And then we have
literally 80 customers

00:25:24.074 --> 00:25:25.740
in the implementation,
and close to six,

00:25:25.740 --> 00:25:28.110
seven customers live,
and I think every week

00:25:28.110 --> 00:25:29.695
and every hour I
will say, they're

00:25:29.695 --> 00:25:31.910
in the progress where
we are signing in.

00:25:31.910 --> 00:25:33.900
So I think the
overall experience

00:25:33.900 --> 00:25:36.920
in terms of-- for sure
I think for the context,

00:25:36.920 --> 00:25:40.470
it is the best fiber-class
network security perspective.

00:25:40.470 --> 00:25:42.659
In terms of cost to the
business, it's great.

00:25:42.659 --> 00:25:44.450
But I would say I think
it's a partnership.

00:25:44.450 --> 00:25:48.780
When we needed Google, I
got everyone available.

00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:50.750
It's not like you have
to go to Diane Greene.

00:25:50.750 --> 00:25:53.660
At the end of the day, I think
it's the people and engineers

00:25:53.660 --> 00:25:54.260
who work.

00:25:54.260 --> 00:25:56.510
I think everyone was available
from an executive layer

00:25:56.510 --> 00:25:58.460
to the Google technical
layer, and I believe

00:25:58.460 --> 00:25:59.584
they are really smart guys.

00:25:59.584 --> 00:26:00.622
When you talk to them--

00:26:00.622 --> 00:26:02.330
and one of the stars,
she's just joining.

00:26:02.330 --> 00:26:03.590
She is late, but I excuse her.

00:26:08.430 --> 00:26:13.500
And I think we are on this
transformation business,

00:26:13.500 --> 00:26:15.710
and I think we are
still not done.

00:26:15.710 --> 00:26:18.010
Every year when we come
here, our eyes got opened.

00:26:18.010 --> 00:26:19.610
OK, we thought we
are doing great.

00:26:19.610 --> 00:26:20.720
We're are on the
SaaS first, but when

00:26:20.720 --> 00:26:22.490
Google shows us,
here is the next five

00:26:22.490 --> 00:26:23.840
years where you will go.

00:26:23.840 --> 00:26:27.680
So we tied them again, and
focused on projects again

00:26:27.680 --> 00:26:29.830
where, how can we
improve the services.

00:26:29.830 --> 00:26:32.090
And at the end of the day,
it is for our customers.

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:34.480
I think what we have
to learn from Google,

00:26:34.480 --> 00:26:37.160
that even though Kronos was
small and Google was big,

00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:40.332
they gave us that level
of support to understand,

00:26:40.332 --> 00:26:42.290
and I think that's what
we are trying to learn.

00:26:42.290 --> 00:26:44.660
There are also customers--

00:26:44.660 --> 00:26:47.020
like, be the customer,
customer's consciousness,

00:26:47.020 --> 00:26:49.670
customer experience, and
the opportunity drivers.

00:26:49.670 --> 00:26:52.370
And then we should partner up
by leveraging the technology

00:26:52.370 --> 00:26:53.580
and build it out.

00:26:53.580 --> 00:26:56.540
So to me, I think standing today
here I could say very firmly,

00:26:56.540 --> 00:26:58.690
and I feel proud that three
years back the decision

00:26:58.690 --> 00:27:00.890
we made, and today where
we are with Google journey.

00:27:00.890 --> 00:27:03.500
And I can tell you, like,
three hours back I had

00:27:03.500 --> 00:27:04.860
10 [INAUDIBLE] I was seeing.

00:27:04.860 --> 00:27:07.070
Today Google Cloud is
everywhere, you know?

00:27:07.070 --> 00:27:09.125
It's getting [? short ?] of it.

00:27:09.125 --> 00:27:11.540
So the experience for
Kronos, I think, overall

00:27:11.540 --> 00:27:15.714
from our engining, we
build our software there

00:27:15.714 --> 00:27:17.630
and we build software
in a very different way,

00:27:17.630 --> 00:27:18.740
by challenging even Google.

00:27:18.740 --> 00:27:20.740
There are some times
that-- how can you leverage

00:27:20.740 --> 00:27:22.580
this infrastructure to build?

00:27:22.580 --> 00:27:25.010
And then we also have
customers running--

00:27:25.010 --> 00:27:26.660
large customers
running in a system,

00:27:26.660 --> 00:27:29.990
where not only here I would
tell you customers running from

00:27:29.990 --> 00:27:33.620
an international location
hosted in the US with fantastic

00:27:33.620 --> 00:27:34.670
latencies--

00:27:34.670 --> 00:27:36.800
fantastic response time.

00:27:36.800 --> 00:27:38.640
So I think our experience
has been great,

00:27:38.640 --> 00:27:40.306
and I think we are
on the learning curve

00:27:40.306 --> 00:27:42.320
by learning from our
customers sitting here,

00:27:42.320 --> 00:27:45.642
and then also learning from
Google by getting more inputs.

00:27:45.642 --> 00:27:47.100
So it has been a
fantastic journey.

00:27:47.100 --> 00:27:49.059
I would like to thank
all the Google, plus also

00:27:49.059 --> 00:27:50.683
all the customers
who have been patient

00:27:50.683 --> 00:27:52.190
and are giving us
this opportunity.

00:27:52.190 --> 00:27:55.460
You don't get an opportunity
to redo a software again

00:27:55.460 --> 00:27:56.220
and again.

00:27:56.220 --> 00:27:58.160
It's a lifetime opportunity.

00:27:58.160 --> 00:27:58.810
So I'll pause.

00:27:58.810 --> 00:28:00.080
I know we've finished.

00:28:00.080 --> 00:28:01.350
We have time for questions.

00:28:01.350 --> 00:28:03.140
I would still request
if you can ask here.

00:28:03.140 --> 00:28:05.067
If you can't, I don't
want to bother you.

00:28:05.067 --> 00:28:06.650
If you are in a
recliner, you're open,

00:28:06.650 --> 00:28:08.175
I can take your questions.

00:28:13.510 --> 00:28:16.030
AUDIENCE: So when is
this infrastructure

00:28:16.030 --> 00:28:18.070
going to be available for
smaller organizations,

00:28:18.070 --> 00:28:22.480
like from your
Workforce Ready product?

00:28:22.480 --> 00:28:23.860
This is D5, is that right?

00:28:23.860 --> 00:28:25.155
GAURAV JETLY: That is correct.

00:28:25.155 --> 00:28:30.780
AUDIENCE: Is there a roadmap
or plan for those users

00:28:30.780 --> 00:28:32.290
using Workforce Ready?

00:28:32.290 --> 00:28:33.331
GAURAV JETLY: Absolutely.

00:28:33.331 --> 00:28:35.820
So part of this offering, we
chose [INAUDIBLE]---- in fact,

00:28:35.820 --> 00:28:38.287
I don't know whether Veronica
asked you this question,

00:28:38.287 --> 00:28:40.620
because she is asking me every
time when Ready is coming

00:28:40.620 --> 00:28:42.240
to Google.

00:28:42.240 --> 00:28:44.760
So just to repeat a
question, so Workforce Ready

00:28:44.760 --> 00:28:46.470
is one of our requisition--

00:28:46.470 --> 00:28:49.090
[INAUDIBLE] is another
product, which is fantastic,

00:28:49.090 --> 00:28:52.110
which is for our small and
medium industry scale--

00:28:52.110 --> 00:28:54.960
not hosted in Google,
but a SaaS product,

00:28:54.960 --> 00:28:56.430
does pretty well in business.

00:28:56.430 --> 00:28:59.820
So part of the transformation--

00:28:59.820 --> 00:29:01.456
our approach was that--

00:29:01.456 --> 00:29:03.330
you have to understand,
an enterprise company

00:29:03.330 --> 00:29:05.310
coming to public cloud
world three years back,

00:29:05.310 --> 00:29:07.050
I can't tell you how I have
to convince my executive

00:29:07.050 --> 00:29:08.950
to be there, but I
think they accepted.

00:29:08.950 --> 00:29:12.540
So we have a success path here
with damage in the building

00:29:12.540 --> 00:29:15.880
out in Google by leveraging
the platform-agnostic model,

00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:17.610
and it's already
in our pipelines

00:29:17.610 --> 00:29:19.922
where soon we'll be
leveraging the same for Ready.

00:29:19.922 --> 00:29:22.380
From a customer perspective,
whether you use Google or not,

00:29:22.380 --> 00:29:24.510
what you see is the
product available.

00:29:24.510 --> 00:29:27.960
But I think we already
have work in progress,

00:29:27.960 --> 00:29:30.710
and very soon you will see it
will be available there, too.

00:29:30.710 --> 00:29:33.476
From our perspective,
I think we don't

00:29:33.476 --> 00:29:35.350
want to get into the
infrastructure business.

00:29:35.350 --> 00:29:37.540
We want to focus on
our domain business,

00:29:37.540 --> 00:29:38.950
and enhance user experience.

00:29:38.950 --> 00:29:40.560
And these guys are spending
billions of dollars.

00:29:40.560 --> 00:29:42.280
Let them do it, and
give us that service.

00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:47.630
So I think we have a
successful Dimension,

00:29:47.630 --> 00:29:49.452
and we want to carry
on with others also.

00:29:49.452 --> 00:29:51.160
So soon you should
see it will be coming.

00:29:51.160 --> 00:29:53.610
It's already on the pipeline.

00:29:53.610 --> 00:29:56.660
[MUSIC PLAYING]

